From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:07:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: the APU monitor submits what the VP produced,
 paced by the device

mcpx_apu_monitor_frame cleared frame_buf every eighth APU frame and refilled
it with the test tone and the HLE software mixer only, overwriting the 256
samples mcpx_apu_dsp_frame had just written from the VP's mixbins, and it
submitted 1,024 (XAudio2) or 2,048 (waveOut) samples for every 256 made. So
no voice the VP played was ever heard.

Now the tone and the mixer are mixed on top of the VP's samples when they're
on, exactly those 256 samples are submitted (XAudio2: one buffer each, a ring
of 16; waveOut: eight frames per buffer), and frame_buf is cleared after the
submit, so a frame whose pipeline didn't run stays silent.

Pacing: with a device, the throttle waits for its queue (fewer than 6 frames
queued), as xemu's monitor queue does. The wall-clock throttle waits in
timer quanta (15.6 ms by default) and restarts when late, so it made
40-45 kHz and the device ran dry 12-30 times a second. It stays as the
no-device fallback. An [APU-OUT] line every 10 s counts frames, underruns
and drops: 48.0 kHz, no underruns, from splash to hub in Crash.

Never pushed: a rule refinement for one title, recorded in the Crash notes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
